{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2622916","formula":"C₁₉H₂₁NO₃","hill":"C19H21NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Nalorphine","ru":"Налорфин","uk":"Налорфін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Nalorphine (INNTooltip International Nonproprietary Name; also known as N-allylnormorphine; brand names Lethidrone and Nalline) is a mixed opioid agonist–antagonist with opioid antagonist and analgesic properties. It was introduced in 1954 and was used as an antidote to reverse opioid overdose and in a challenge test to determine opioid dependence. Nalorphine was the second opioid antagonist to be introduced, preceded by nalodeine (N-allylnorcodeine) in 1915 and followed by naloxone in 1960 and naltrexone in 1963.","ru":"Налорфи́н (Nalorphini hydrochloridum — N-аллилнорморфина гидрохлорид) — агонист-антагонист опиоидных рецепторов. Синонимы: Анторфин, Anarcon, Lethidron, Nalorphine hydrochloride, Nalline, Norfin и др.","uk":"Налорфін (лат. Nalorphinum, англ. Nalorphine; Lethidrone, Nalline) — напівсинтетичний лікарський засіб, що є структурним аналогом опіоїдних анальгетиків (за хімічною структурою близький до морфіну), та застосовується у низці країн як антидот при передозуванні опіоїдів."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":5284595,"mass":311.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C=CCN1CC[C@]23[C@@H]4[C@H]1CC5=C2C(=C(C=C5)O)O[C@H]3[C@H](C=C4)O","inchikey":"UIQMVEYFGZJHCZ-SSTWWWIQSA-N","iupac":"(4R,4aR,7S,7aR,12bS)-3-prop-2-enyl-2,4,4a,7,7a,13-hexahydro-1H-4,12-methanobenzofuro[3,2-e]isoquinoline-7,9-diol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5284595","atoms":44,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.351,"y":-0.125,"z":1.419,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.635,"y":-2.096,"z":0.285,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.693,"y":2.379,"z":0.819,"el":"O"},{"x":2.665,"y":-0.533,"z":-0.